rt of Elizabeth I as never known before History has pictured Elizabeth I as Gloriana, an icon of strength and power. But the reality, especially during her later years, was not so simple. In 1583 Elizabeth is fifty years old, but her greatest challenges are still to come: the Spanish Armada; the execution of Mary, Queen of Scots; relentless plotting among her courtiers. This gripping and vivid portrait of her life and times - often told in her own words ('You know I am no morning woman') - reveals a woman who is fallible, increasingly insecure, and struggling to lead Britain. This is the real Elizabeth, for the first time. ____________________ 'One of the very best historians we have in the country . . .","pageCount":425,"publicationYear":2016,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"Biography & Autobiography","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-elizabeth-the-forgotten-years-john-guy"}],"displaySummary":"In 1583 Elizabeth is fifty years old, but her greatest challenges are still to come: the Spanish Armada; the execution of Mary, Queen of Scots; relentless plotting among her courtiers. This gripping and vivid portrait of her life and times - often told in her own words ('You know I am no morning woman') - reveals a woman who is fallible, increasingly insecure, and struggling to lead Britain. This is the real Elizabeth, for the first time. ____________________ 'One of the very best historians we have in the country . . .","primaryTopic":"Courts & Trials","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Biography","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Biography","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Biography","mappedSubject":"Biography","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book is a detailed biography of Queen Elizabeth I, primarily focusing on her life and political challenges in her final years, thus fitting best under Biography with a secondar